## Previously raised findings (review-round registry)

These defects were raised on earlier review rounds of this PR. For each finding below: verify fixed (cite the fixing hunk), withdraw (reason required), or mark re-introduced. New claims need new evidence — a claim already on this list is answered, not re-raised.

| id | status | severity | file | claim |
|----|--------|----------|------|-------|
| F1 | open | BLOCKING | .github/workflows/fix-in-flight.yml | 🚨 blocking fix in flight yml will fail at actions checkout — the top level permissions block grants no contents read the workflow declares only issues write at the top level lines 30–31 per github s permissions semantics once a permissions block is present every unspecified scope is set to none — so contents is none here while the very first step is actions checkout line 43 actions checkout requires contents read to fetch the repository without it the step fails with resource not accessible by integration and the run dies before scripts fix in flight marker sh ever executes the workflow file s own header comment cites the 624 625 startup failure class as the reason for staying standalone — this permission omission reintroduces exactly that class every opened reopened closed event on any pr will produce a red x run and ac1 s label comment marker will never be stamped or cleared the wiring test in test machine kit fix in flight marker test dart pins permissions issues write but asserts nothing about contents so the suite stays green while the workflow is dead — which is how this slipped through fix add contents read to the top level permissions block minimal grant matching the repo s sec 08 minimal permission pattern used in ai teammate yml s gate job yaml permissions contents read actions checkout issues write label comment on the issue and extend the wiring test to pin perms contents read so a regression here turns red instead of red xing every pr event |
| F2 | open | IMPORTANT | scripts/teammate_picker.sh | ⚠️ important the skip notice is printed to stdout so the gate s leg output is polluted — ac2 s skipped with an empty leg contract does not hold on the skip path the script does bash echo notice title fix in flight issue issue already has an open referencing pr exit 0 with no 2 in github workflows ai teammate yml the gate captures the picker s stdout yaml leg bash scripts teammate picker sh issue number echo leg leg github output so on a skip leg is the literal notice title fix in flight issue n text and github output gets leg notice title — not the empty value ac2 and the pr description promise skipped with an empty leg the annotation also never renders workflow commands only become annotations when printed by the step itself and this one is captured into a variable the factory reusable workflow then receives the notice text as its leg input this repo cannot verify how dmtools agentic workflows factory teammate yml treats an unexpected leg value — if it dispatches on exact matches it degrades to a silent no op but the sibling human assignee standby path in this same workflow line 151 deliberately writes a genuinely empty leg so the two skip paths now behave differently note the fail closed lookup error path two lines above already gets this right 2 and the dart harness happens to mask the bug teammate picker test dart derives the leg as out startswith dev dev so the polluted output still reads as skip in tests fix send the notice to stderr matching the fail closed path bash echo notice title fix in flight 2 exit 0 stdout then carries only the dev decision or nothing optionally pin this in the gate wiring test by asserting the workflow s command substitution consumes stdout only |

### How to answer

Add a `findingReview` block to `outputs/pr_review.json` (alongside `inlineComments`):

```json
{"findingReview": {
  "dispositions": [
    {"n": 1, "status": "fixed", "hunk": "<file:lines \u2014 the fixing hunk>"},
    {"n": 2, "status": "withdrawn", "reason": "<why this is not a defect>"},
    {"n": 3, "status": "re-introduced"}
  ],
  "confirmations": [
    {"proposedFor": 1, "same": true}
  ]
}}
```

Unconfirmed candidates become new identities (the merge bias is confirm-only); a genuinely new finding on a resolved item is expected to be raised again with new evidence.

